---Represents a textual expression in the Common Expression Language (CEL) syntax. CEL is a C-like expression language. The syntax and semantics of CEL are documented at https://github.com/google/cel-spec. Example (Comparison): title: "Summary size limit" description: "Determines if a summary is less than 100 chars" expression: "document.summary.size() < 100" Example (Equality): title: "Requestor is owner" description: "Determines if requestor is the document owner" expression: "document.owner == request.auth.claims.email" Example (Logic): title: "Public documents" description: "Determine whether the document should be publicly visible" expression: "document.type != 'private' && document.type != 'internal'" Example (Data Manipulation): title: "Notification string" description: "Create a notification string with a timestamp." expression: "'New message received at ' + string(document.create_time)" The exact variables and functions that may be referenced within an expression are determined by the service that evaluates it. See the service documentation for additional information.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.Expr
---@field expression? string Textual representation of an expression in Common Expression Language syntax.
---@field location? string Optional. String indicating the location of the expression for error reporting, e.g. a file name and a position in the file.
---@field description? string Optional. Description of the expression. This is a longer text which describes the expression, e.g. when hovered over it in a UI.
---@field title? string Optional. Title for the expression, i.e. a short string describing its purpose. This can be used e.g. in UIs which allow to enter the expression.

---For display only. Metadata associated with a VPC firewall rule, an implied VPC firewall rule, or a firewall policy rule.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.FirewallInfo
---@field action? string Possible values: ALLOW, DENY, APPLY_SECURITY_PROFILE_GROUP
---@field targetTags? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.StringList The target tags defined by the VPC firewall rule. This field is not applicable to firewall policy rules.
---@field direction? string Possible values: INGRESS, EGRESS
---@field targetType? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.FirewallInfoTargetTypeEnum|string Target type of the firewall rule.
---@field policy? string The name of the firewall policy that this rule is associated with. This field is not applicable to VPC firewall rules and implied VPC firewall rules.
---@field targetServiceAccounts? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.StringList The target service accounts specified by the firewall rule.
---@field firewallRuleType? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.FirewallInfoFirewallRuleTypeEnum|string The firewall rule's type.
---@field displayName? string The display name of the firewall rule. This field might be empty for firewall policy rules.
---@field priority? number The priority of the firewall rule.
---@field policyUri? string The URI of the firewall policy that this rule is associated with. This field is not applicable to VPC firewall rules and implied VPC firewall rules. Format: * `locations/global/firewallPolicies/{policy}` (hierarchical policy) * `projects/{project}/global/firewallPolicies/{policy}` (global network firewall policy) * `projects/{project}/regions/{region}/firewallPolicies/{policy}`
---@field policyPriority? number The priority of the firewall policy that this rule is associated with. This field is not applicable to VPC firewall rules and implied VPC firewall rules.
---@field networkUri? string The URI of the VPC network that the firewall rule is associated with in format "projects/{project}/global/networks/{network}". This field is not applicable to hierarchical firewall policy rules.
