---This resource represents a long-running operation that is the result of a network API call.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.Operation
---@field response? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.DocumentMap The normal, successful response of the operation. If the original method returns no data on success, such as `Delete`, the response is `google.protobuf.Empty`. If the original method is standard `Get`/`Create`/`Update`, the response should be the resource. For other methods, the response should have the type `XxxResponse`, where `Xxx` is the original method name. For example, if the original method name is `TakeSnapshot()`, the inferred response type is `TakeSnapshotResponse`.
---@field done? boolean If the value is `false`, it means the operation is still in progress. If `true`, the operation is completed, and either `error` or `response` is available.
---@field name? string The server-assigned name, which is only unique within the same service that originally returns it. If you use the default HTTP mapping, the `name` should be a resource name ending with `operations/{unique_id}`.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.DocumentMap Service-specific metadata associated with the operation. It typically contains progress information and common metadata such as create time. Some services might not provide such metadata. Any method that returns a long-running operation should document the metadata type, if any.
---@field error? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.Status The error result of the operation in case of failure or cancellation.

---@alias gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.OperationList gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.Operation[]

---@class gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.PatchOrganizationsLocationsVpcFlowLogsConfigsRequest
---@field metadataFields? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Custom metadata fields to include in the reported VPC flow logs. Can only be specified if "metadata" was set to CUSTOM_METADATA.
---@field description? string Optional. The user-supplied description of the VPC Flow Logs configuration. Maximum of 512 characters.
---@field interconnectAttachment? string Traffic will be logged from the Interconnect Attachment. Format: projects/{project_id}/regions/{region}/interconnectAttachments/{name}
---@field state? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.VpcFlowLogsConfigStateEnum|string Optional. The state of the VPC Flow Log configuration. Default value is ENABLED. When creating a new configuration, it must be enabled. Setting state=DISABLED will pause the log generation for this config.
---@field filterExpr? string Optional. Export filter used to define which VPC Flow Logs should be logged.
---@field network? string Traffic will be logged from VMs, VPN tunnels and Interconnect Attachments within the network. Format: projects/{project_id}/global/networks/{name}
---@field flowSampling? number Optional. The value of the field must be in (0, 1]. The sampling rate of VPC Flow Logs where 1.0 means all collected logs are reported. Setting the sampling rate to 0.0 is not allowed. If you want to disable VPC Flow Logs, use the state field instead. Default value is 1.0.
---@field vpnTunnel? string Traffic will be logged from the VPN Tunnel. Format: projects/{project_id}/regions/{region}/vpnTunnels/{name}
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time the config was created.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time the config was updated.
---@field crossProjectMetadata? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.VpcFlowLogsConfigCrossProjectMetadataEnum|string Optional. Determines whether to include cross project annotations in the logs. This field is available only for organization configurations. If not specified in org configs will be set to CROSS_PROJECT_METADATA_ENABLED.
---@field connectionLogging? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.VpcFlowLogsConfigConnectionLoggingEnum|string Optional. Configures whether connection logging is enabled for VPC Flow Logs.
---@field aggregationInterval? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.VpcFlowLogsConfigAggregationIntervalEnum|string Optional. The aggregation interval for the logs. Default value is INTERVAL_5_SEC.
---@field targetResourceState? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.VpcFlowLogsConfigTargetResourceStateEnum|string Output only. Describes the state of the configured target resource for diagnostic purposes.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Resource labels to represent user-provided metadata.
---@field subnet? string Traffic will be logged from VMs within the subnetwork. Format: projects/{project_id}/regions/{region}/subnetworks/{name}
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.VpcFlowLogsConfigMetadataEnum|string Optional. Configures whether all, none or a subset of metadata fields should be added to the reported VPC flow logs. Default value is INCLUDE_ALL_METADATA.
---@field updateMask? string Required. Mask of fields to update. At least one path must be supplied in this field. For example, to change the state of the configuration to ENABLED, specify `update_mask` = `"state"`, and the `vpc_flow_logs_config` would be: `vpc_flow_logs_config = { name = "projects/my-project/locations/global/vpcFlowLogsConfigs/my-config" state = "ENABLED" }`
---@field name string Identifier. Unique name of the configuration. The name can have one of the following forms: - For project-level configurations: `projects/{project_id}/locations/global/vpcFlowLogsConfigs/{vpc_flow_logs_config_id}` - For organization-level configurations: `organizations/{organization_id}/locations/global/vpcFlowLogsConfigs/{vpc_flow_logs_config_id}`

