---A configuration to generate VPC Flow Logs.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.VpcFlowLogsConfig
---@field metadataFields? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Custom metadata fields to include in the reported VPC flow logs. Can only be specified if "metadata" was set to CUSTOM_METADATA.
---@field description? string Optional. The user-supplied description of the VPC Flow Logs configuration. Maximum of 512 characters.
---@field interconnectAttachment? string Traffic will be logged from the Interconnect Attachment. Format: projects/{project_id}/regions/{region}/interconnectAttachments/{name}
---@field state? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.VpcFlowLogsConfigStateEnum Optional. The state of the VPC Flow Log configuration. Default value is ENABLED. When creating a new configuration, it must be enabled. Setting state=DISABLED will pause the log generation for this config.
---@field filterExpr? string Optional. Export filter used to define which VPC Flow Logs should be logged.
---@field network? string Traffic will be logged from VMs, VPN tunnels and Interconnect Attachments within the network. Format: projects/{project_id}/global/networks/{name}
---@field flowSampling? number Optional. The value of the field must be in (0, 1]. The sampling rate of VPC Flow Logs where 1.0 means all collected logs are reported. Setting the sampling rate to 0.0 is not allowed. If you want to disable VPC Flow Logs, use the state field instead. Default value is 1.0.
---@field vpnTunnel? string Traffic will be logged from the VPN Tunnel. Format: projects/{project_id}/regions/{region}/vpnTunnels/{name}
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time the config was created.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time the config was updated.
---@field crossProjectMetadata? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.VpcFlowLogsConfigCrossProjectMetadataEnum Optional. Determines whether to include cross project annotations in the logs. This field is available only for organization configurations. If not specified in org configs will be set to CROSS_PROJECT_METADATA_ENABLED.
---@field name? string Identifier. Unique name of the configuration. The name can have one of the following forms: - For project-level configurations: `projects/{project_id}/locations/global/vpcFlowLogsConfigs/{vpc_flow_logs_config_id}` - For organization-level configurations: `organizations/{organization_id}/locations/global/vpcFlowLogsConfigs/{vpc_flow_logs_config_id}`
---@field connectionLogging? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.VpcFlowLogsConfigConnectionLoggingEnum Optional. Configures whether connection logging is enabled for VPC Flow Logs.
---@field aggregationInterval? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.VpcFlowLogsConfigAggregationIntervalEnum Optional. The aggregation interval for the logs. Default value is INTERVAL_5_SEC.
---@field targetResourceState? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.VpcFlowLogsConfigTargetResourceStateEnum Output only. Describes the state of the configured target resource for diagnostic purposes.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Resource labels to represent user-provided metadata.
---@field subnet? string Traffic will be logged from VMs within the subnetwork. Format: projects/{project_id}/regions/{region}/subnetworks/{name}
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.VpcFlowLogsConfigMetadataEnum Optional. Configures whether all, none or a subset of metadata fields should be added to the reported VPC flow logs. Default value is INCLUDE_ALL_METADATA.

---@alias gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.VpcFlowLogsConfigAggregationIntervalEnum "AGGREGATION_INTERVAL_UNSPECIFIED"|"INTERVAL_5_SEC"|"INTERVAL_30_SEC"|"INTERVAL_1_MIN"|"INTERVAL_5_MIN"|"INTERVAL_10_MIN"|"INTERVAL_15_MIN"

---@alias gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.VpcFlowLogsConfigConnectionLoggingEnum "CONNECTION_LOGGING_UNSPECIFIED"|"CONNECTION_LOGGING_ENABLED"|"CONNECTION_LOGGING_DISABLED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.networkmanagement_v1beta1.VpcFlowLogsConfigCrossProjectMetadataEnum "CROSS_PROJECT_METADATA_UNSPECIFIED"|"CROSS_PROJECT_METADATA_ENABLED"|"CROSS_PROJECT_METADATA_DISABLED"

